0 FILE triceratops.ldr
0 BRICK Triceratops 77985 reconstruction draft
0 Name: triceratops-v0.mpd
0 Evidence printed pages 148–149 / steps 278–279: two-pin link is assembled internally, then docked to the anterior torso. Provisional port roles: 32184 crosshole toward skull; remaining 32140 hole toward torso. Exact mating identities remain unverified.
0 The step-278 link is a local submodel. Step279 docks its remaining 32140 hole provisionally to the torso; the orthogonal 32184 port is provisionally skull-side. Step247/249 receiver identities and engagement remain uncertain. Independent base steps 280–284 are modeled locally.
0 Author: BRICK project
0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","model":"Triceratops fossil reconstruction","reference_set":"LEGO 77985","reference_url":"https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6649862.pdf","manual_files":["6649862-1.pdf","6649862-2.pdf"],"progress_note":"Steps 247–249 torso candidates and the step278 link remain local. Step278 has two internal 11214 pins; based on the 278→279 sequence 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so torso alignment does not require both orthogonal ports. User retained 6577/43093 and parallel/orthogonal alternatives as uncertain; no repeat question. Independent base steps 280–286 are modeled, with step284 3021/3022 identities supported by the callout and placements provisional.","piece_count":66,"unique_sale_skus":7,"listed_retail_parts_cost_cny":"0.95","cost_scope":"Not totaled; candidate mappings only.","target_dimensions_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"reference_geometry_bounds_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"support_count":0,"support_verification":"Not assessed.","validation":{"instruction_scope":"printed page 136 step247; page137 step249; page142 step263; printed pages 143–149 steps264–279: body mount and skull docking callouts inspected; printed p150 steps280–281: separate base strip started; printed p151 step282: tile cover added; printed p151 step283: 1x2 plate, Technic brick, and dual-finger hinge candidates placed; printed p151 step284: one 2x3 plate and one 2x2 plate added to independent base; printed p151 step285: two double-curved slope shape candidates placed; printed p152 step286 and p153 side views: paired large triangular panels registered as 30355/30356 shape candidates","placements":"Step278 internal two-pin fit: official DAT centerlines have 0 LDU transverse residual and 20 LDU face spacing; the nominal 11214 pin sections span their 32140/32184 bores. Step247 6541 hole center [20,20,20], axis +Y, is coaxial with the free 32140 port and its adjoining face; the two 6577 candidates are stacked vertically below the 6541, not placed through the side hole. Step249 support holes are 20 LDU apart and their candidate 43093/62462 axes are aligned; actual pin depth and whether the second 6541 axis is parallel or orthogonal remain unresolved; the user retained both candidates. 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so the receiver is not required to align with both axes. Step279 has no parts in its callout; the required sockets must pre-exist on the body. Step280 base strip uses a 2x10 plate with a 50340 dual-finger hinge candidate across its end; step281 has paired 1x3 plates on adjacent rows. These are independent local coordinates and remain diagram-based pending later platform stages. Official candidate port calculations: step249 6541 axes are both +Z and 20 LDU apart; each 43093 and the near hole of each 62462 are coaxial. The currently modeled far sockets are [390,-14,50] and [410,-14,50], both +Z. Step278 link has two remaining external candidates with +Y and +Z axes; the step278 ports now have separate provisional roles: 32184 toward the skull and the remaining 32140 hole toward the torso, following step279 docking order. Therefore the torso receiver need not fit both orthogonal axes. Keep the step249 parallel/orthogonal axis question local and unresolved; do not reject its candidate from a two-port mismatch alone. Step282 tile 2x4 is placed over the hinge-end studs as a diagram-based provisional cover. Step283 candidate rows use two official DAT height registrations: 3023b row at 8 LDU, 3700 row at 24 LDU, with 50340 plates stacked at the corresponding top levels. Finger direction and exact rows remain provisional. Step284 adds one 3021 2x3 plate and one 3022 2x2 plate to the independent base; IDs and official DAT shapes are registered, while exact overlap/row remain provisional. Step285 adds two 1762 double-curved slope shape candidates based on callout curvature and count; exact ID/orientation and stud footprint remain unverified. Step286 places one 30355/30356 mirrored 6x12-wing shape candidate on either side of the base; footprint and scale follow the manual, but mold allocation, hinge contact and engagement height remain tentative.","catalog_and_asset_references":"official LDraw parts 32140, 32184, 98989, 11214 inspected; GoBricks SKU mappings remain unverified","full_connection_graph":"Step278 11214 pair is consumed internally between 32184 and the two connected 32140 holes. The remaining 32140 hole is the provisional torso-side port because step279 docks the completed link to the anterior torso; the 32184 orthogonal crosshole is the provisional skull-side port. These port-role assignments follow assembly order but remain subject to exact contact-part confirmation. A torso receiver is not required to satisfy both axes. The 247 single-hole candidate has 0 LDU transverse axis residual and 0 LDU face gap to the 32140 port; this is coordinate registration only. Step249’s paired support remains a candidate and its connection role/transform is unresolved.","exact_mesh_collision":"unverified_open_surface_probe_ambiguous","physical_build":"not_tested","mesh_collision_note":"A Blender Boolean probe was attempted after recursively triangulating LDraw DAT references. The flattened 32140 mesh retained 148 non-manifold edges of 2762; 32184 retained 360/2170; 11214 retained 383/1378; 6541 retained 56/520. Intersection volumes were nonzero small artifacts even for intended face contacts, so these booleans cannot establish collision-free fit. Use only the independently computed hole-axis/face-spacing checks until watertight solid reconstruction is available. The later step249 candidate probe likewise showed intersecting triangles at intended pin/receiver, joiner/pin and plate/brick interfaces; no valid solid-overlap result was produced.","surface_collision_note":"Open-triangle BVH tests were run on unmodified official LDraw meshes after the initial 278 link and again on the step249 candidate support. The 249 test reported intersections/zero nearest-surface distance at 6541↔43093, 43093↔62462, plate↔brick, and adjacent brick contacts. This watertightness-independent surface check cannot distinguish intended contact/friction engagement from penetration and cannot test containment. Result is ambiguous/unverified, not a collision-free pass. Keep separate from closed-solid Boolean probes, which were invalidated by non-manifold input.","open_questions":[{"id":"step247-small-round-parts","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":136,"step":247,"candidates":["6577.dat Technic Bush 1/2 Type 2","43093.dat Technic Axle Pin with Friction"],"evidence":"P136 exploded callout shows two small ring-like parts in a vertical stack below a 6541 candidate. 6577 has a female axle bore and fits the ring silhouette but requires an underlying shaft; 43093 has a male friction-pin form that can enter the 6541 side hole but is inconsistent with the depicted vertical spacer placement.","needed":"Do not ask again. Resolve only if a later manual view, parts inventory, or actual mating geometry distinguishes female 6577 from male 43093; otherwise retain local candidate status."},{"id":"step249-receiver-axis","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":137,"step":249,"candidates":["parallel 6541 hole axes","orthogonal 6541 hole axes"],"evidence":"The user asked to retain both orientations while uncertain. 32184 is provisionally skull-side and the remaining 32140 port torso-side, so the torso receiver need not align to both link axes. Parallel/orthogonal comparison alone does not eliminate either receiver candidate.","needed":"Do not ask again. Use a later reverse-side manual view or corroborating support geometry if it becomes available; otherwise keep this axis detail deferred."}]},"nodes":{"skull-torso-link":{"origin":"midpoint between the two registered 32140 beam-hole centers; local +Y is their shared axis; local Z separation is 40 LDU","root_transform_status":"local subassembly only; global transform withheld until skull and torso mating datums are measured","remaining_32140_hole_candidate":{"center":[20,0,20],"axis":[0,1,0],"candidate_receiver":"6541.dat","receiver_hole_center":[20,20,20],"receiver_axis":[0,1,0],"transverse_residual_ldu":0,"face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"diagram_based_tentative; assigned as the single torso-side port candidate from the step278→279 assembly sequence; exact receiver, part identity and insertion depth remain unconfirmed"},"link_ports":{"beam_free_hole_candidate":{"part":"32140.dat","center":[20,0,20],"axis":[0,1,0],"role":"provisional torso-side port: step279 docks this completed link to the anterior torso; this is the remaining 32140 hole, subject to exact receiver confirmation"},"crossblock_crosshole_candidate":{"part":"32184.dat","center":[0,20,0],"axis":[0,0,1],"role":"provisional skull-side port: 32184 is the compact cross block on the skull-side end of the step278 link; mating skull part/pin remains unverified"},"bridge_pins":{"part":"11214.dat","count":2,"centerline_z":[-20,20],"axis":[0,1,0],"role":"official-DAT-fit axle sections seat 20 LDU into 32184; pin sections traverse 32140; they join the two link pieces, not yet assigned to an external endpoint"}},"two_port_test":{"step278_roles":"32184 orthogonal crosshole is the provisional skull-side port; 32140 remaining hole is the provisional torso-side port, based on link topology and step279 docking sequence.","geometry":"The body-side receiver need only align to the 32140 port if the 32184 end belongs to the skull. Do not reject a torso receiver based on requiring it to match both +Y and +Z ports.","step249_parallel_candidate":{"centers":[[390,-14,50],[410,-14,50]],"axes":[[0,0,1],[0,0,1]],"pitch_ldu":20,"status":"retain as a candidate body support; its two outlets are not both required to mate to the torso if only the 32140 port is body-side. Exact port correspondence, transform and insertion remain unresolved."},"step247_single_port_candidate":{"link_center":[20,0,20],"link_axis":[0,1,0],"receiver_center":[20,20,20],"receiver_axis":[0,1,0],"transverse_residual_ldu":0,"face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"coordinate/axis registration only; receiver identity and mechanical engagement are not confirmed"}}},"independent-base-280":{"origin":"local datum at center of 2x10 plate, isolated at world X=600 to keep it independent from torso/skull fragments","parts":[{"id":"part-0052","part":"3832.dat","role":"2x10 tan base plate; shape/stud count confirmed"},{"id":"part-0053","part":"50340.dat","role":"1x2 dual-finger hinge shape candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0054","part":"3623.dat","role":"first 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0055","part":"3623.dat","role":"second 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0056","part":"87079.dat","role":"step282 2x4 tile cover candidate; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0057","part":"3023b.dat","role":"step283 1x2 plate row; position provisional"},{"id":"part-0058","part":"3700.dat","role":"step283 1x2 Technic brick with two holes; row/orientation provisional"},{"id":"part-0059","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 first dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0060","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 second dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0061","part":"3021.dat","role":"step284 2x3 plate; identity supported by six-stud callout and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0062","part":"3022.dat","role":"step284 2x2 plate; identity supported by four-stud callout/underside and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0063","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 first of two 2x2 double-curved slope candidates; shape/quantity candidate, transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0064","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 second double-curved slope candidate; paired row provisional"},{"id":"part-0065","part":"30355.dat","role":"step286 large studded triangular wing panel; official 6x12 left shape candidate, side/hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0066","part":"30356.dat","role":"step286 mirrored 6x12 right wing panel candidate; exact callout mold allocation and hinge transform provisional"}],"status":"independent subassembly draft; steps 280–286 modeled; step286 wing-to-base hinge engagement provisional"}},"joints":[{"id":"joint-skull-anterior-torso","type":"technic_pin_link_to_technic_mount","from":"completed_skull_rear_connector","to":"anterior_torso_technic_mount","evidence":{"manual_file":"6649862-2.pdf","printed_pages":[148,149],"steps":[278,279]},"connection_status":"instruction_confirmed","connector_parts_status":"geometry-compatible candidates placed: 32140 + 32184 + 2x11214; manual mold identification remains unconfirmed","relative_transform_status":"step_278_link_local_fit_applied; step247 single-port receiver aligned provisionally; step249 parallel-pair candidate fails a two-port axis test against the current +Y/+Z link ports; final pose and receiver variant unresolved","reason":"Step 278 shows two pins added to the black connector at the skull rear; step 279 calls out docking to the anterior torso. The local candidate connector is physically placed and its fit dimensions are recorded. Exact receiver parts and local attachment datums are not yet modeled, so the global transform cannot be derived from the overview alone. A provisional 6541 body-side receiver is placed against the third 32140 hole using official DAT hole center and axis; the callout-visible connection point and any intervening pin remain unconfirmed. Step249 candidate comparison used official LDraw hole axes and centers: current paired outlet axes are parallel, while the two candidate external link ports are orthogonal. Therefore do not claim simultaneous two-port engagement from the current arrangement.","connector_candidates":[{"part":"32140.dat","name":"Technic Beam 2 x 4 Liftarm Bent 90","status":"geometry_candidate_placed","geometry":"Two arm holes at 40-LDU pitch register to the 32184 axle stations; rendered silhouette matches the bent beam callout, but exact manual mold mapping remains unconfirmed."},{"part":"32184.dat","name":"Technic Cross Block 1 x 3 (Axle/Pin/Axle)","status":"geometry_candidate_placed","geometry":"Official axle bores register to the two 32140 holes at 40-LDU pitch; the orthogonal pin-hole remains available for the skull-side connection. Silhouette is consistent but not uniquely legible in the callout."},{"part":"98989.dat","name":"Technic Cross Block 2 x 4 (Axle/Pin/Pin/Twin Pin)","status":"rejected_by_hole_pattern","geometry":"Official 2x4 envelope and multi-hole pattern is larger than the compact two-station cross part shown; no matching two-hole pairing in the compared orientation."}],"alternative_connector_candidate":"98989.dat rejected for this two-station link by size and hole pattern; not retained as a current alternate.","pin_part":"11214.dat x2 geometry candidate; official geometry gives 20 LDU axle section into 32184, 20 LDU pin section within 32140, and 20 LDU exposed. Which endpoint is skull-side remains unresolved.","receiver_candidates":[{"part":"6541.dat","name":"Technic Brick 1 x 1 with Hole","status":"diagram_candidate_placed_tentatively","evidence":"Printed p136 step247 shows a single-hole black Technic brick above a two-piece vertical spacer stack. The official 6541 side-hole center/axis aligns with the third free 32140 bore; the two 6577s are vertical spacer candidates below it, not side-hole inserts. Exact bush mold and hidden lower support axle remain unverified."},{"part":"step249 paired 6541/3023 support","name":"two Technic single-hole blocks held between paired 1x2 plates","status":"local_two_port_candidate_with_axis_mismatch_to_current_link","evidence":"Printed p137 step249 inventory/callout shows two 6541s, plates, two short male-pin candidates and two round slotted joiners. The current official-DAT registration yields parallel +Z socket axes at 20-LDU pitch. The 278 link exposes candidate +Y and +Z ports; both cannot mate to this parallel pair simultaneously. An orthogonal variant or single-port engagement remains possible; the far-side callout does not settle it."}]}],"instances":[{"id":"part-0001","group":"stand","part":"4282.dat","gobricks_id":"517","sku":"GDS-517-031","color":19,"position":[0,0,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 1 tan 2x16 base; datum center."},{"id":"part-0002","group":"stand","part":"36840.dat","gobricks_id":"1567","sku":"GDS-1567-072","color":72,"position":[-140,0,0],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 1 gray inverted bracket near one end; X approximate from diagram."},{"id":"part-0003","group":"stand","part":"3023b.dat","gobricks_id":"502","sku":"GDS-502-081","color":70,"position":[-100,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 2 first reddish-brown 1x2 plate; diagram placement."},{"id":"part-0004","group":"stand","part":"3023b.dat","gobricks_id":"502","sku":"GDS-502-081","color":70,"position":[-80,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 2 second reddish-brown 1x2 plate; stud locations provisional."},{"id":"part-0005","group":"stand","part":"54200.dat","gobricks_id":"833","sku":"GDS-833-081","color":70,"position":[-60,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Manual printed page 11 step 3; inventory visible, exact mold candidate and stud placement provisional."},{"id":"part-0006","group":"stand","part":"36840.dat","gobricks_id":"1567","sku":"GDS-1567-072","color":72,"position":[-20,0,0],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"catalog_mapping_